      "anchor": "/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/reckon/docs/plans/the-monitor-shows-the-work-it-watches.html:709",
      "id": "reasoning-1",
      "reason": "the node needs the plan to say whether the end row's named-run tail goes too (and then the new test must drive a lifetime-elapse case) or why it stays as the one deliberate exception, since without that the section's stated premise is false and its measure is undefined on a live pane path.",
      "text": "the Why asserts that after \u00a783 the settle tail \"is the one place the pane still prints a needs-you list\", but `_follower_end_line` (reckon/crew_follow_commands.py:662-699) composes `\"N runs need you: <run_id> (<node>), \u2026\"` from the same `needs_you` derivation (`_needs_you_runs`, :569), is emitted as `FOLLOWER_END_EVENT` when the arming lifetime elapses (:692-720, yielded at :2560), and is printed verbatim to the pane (:3263-3272 echoes `event[\"line\"]`) \u2014 so a node that implements \u00a793 exactly as written leaves a needs-you list on the pane, and the new test's \"no line naming them is printed\" has no defined answer for that path",
      "type": "reasoning",
      "would_change": true
    },
    {
      "anchor": "/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/reckon/docs/plans/the-monitor-shows-the-work-it-watches.html:709",
      "id": "done_when-1",
      "reason": "without a second declared control (or a stated base run of the new test) the stale-line guard is measured only in the direction that passes, which is the check the section exists to make falsifiable.",
      "text": "the declared negative control restores the settle tail only, while the deliverable's other half (no station-stale line from a subscriber whose heartbeat is 120 s old) is asserted by the new test and nothing shows that assertion can fail: `stale_line` (reckon/crew/station_subscriber.py:521-523, driven at :566) is untouched by the named control, and the base arm compares only the pre-existing importer test files, in which the new test does not exist at base",
      "type": "done_when",
      "would_change": true
    }
  ],
