    "anchors_resolve": "pass \u2014 `_follower_settle_line` (reckon/crew_follow_commands.py:727), `needs_you.drain_tail` (reckon/crew/needs_you.py:292), `stale_heartbeat_line` (reckon/crew/station_subscriber.py:226, `STALE_HEARTBEAT_SECONDS = 90.0` at :42), `_needs_remind_seconds` (:2901) and the `--remind` option (:2978) all resolve at head aa448b01, commit `06467f9da4` exists and is the change cited, `needs_you.needs_you_line` (needs_you.py:352) has only a test caller, all six test files named for rewriting exist and the new test file does not, sibling plan \u00a712 (`docs/plans/work-is-never-stuck-behind-the-admission-loop.html`, `data-id=\"s12\"`, `data-status=\"done\"`) exists and names the slow-station verdict, and `reckon crew view obligations` resolves as a live crew view (reckon/crew/tombstones.py:119).",
    "done_when": "a finding \u2014 the stale-heartbeat half of the deliverable's measure declares no negative control; only the settle tail does.",
    "evidence_paths": "pass \u2014 the measure is a test file at a durable repository path (`tests/test_the_pane_carries_counts_not_names.py`) plus a base-arm comparison and ruff; no session scratchpad or node-local temporary path is named.",
    "naming": "pass \u2014 the new test filename and any symbols it adds carry no plan, stage or ticket label; the \u00a783 and commit references live in plan prose, which is the plan record and not source.",
    "reasoning": "a finding \u2014 the Why's claim that the settle tail is \"the one place the pane still prints a needs-you list\" does not hold at head: the follower's end row composes a second one.",
    "single_goal": "pass \u2014 both removals serve the one goal in the section title (the pane spends a line only on something the reader acts on), and the goal is closed by one new test file.",
    "wiring": "pass \u2014 \u00a793 declares no relationships of its own (`data-links=\"\"`), and the two mechanisms it removes sit in modules it names as write paths (`reckon/crew_follow_commands.py`, `reckon/crew/station_subscriber.py`); no relationship points at the wrong node, and the previously raised \"no followup recommends \u00a793\" finding was declined with a reason and has not changed."
